
the course was dry so let's start talking about zombies and orphans
what happens when an application terminates
  os retains some information of terminated process(so parent can find out reason for exiting.)
  this takes up some memory.
  Calling wait() on a terminated process frees this memory.
Zombie:
  A process state where child process has terminated  
    but the parent process hasn't called `wait()` yet.
      (what happens if child turn into zombies, we just call wait)
    we make zombies and we make orphans

    orphans:
      state where:
        child process is running
        parent process has terminated.
      Orphan processes no longer have  a parent process
    Linux handling of Orphan processes
      Orphan child process become a child process of into
      init calls wait() on all child processes
        init handles orphan zombies.

